"Tandoori roti","dish/tandoori-roti"],["Thali","dish/thali"],["Zarda (food)","dish/zarda-food"]]}],"img":{"src":"/world-cuisine/img/thumb/1/12/Kachumber_Salad.JPG/500px-Kachumber_Salad.JPG","w":500,"h":501,"by":"Miansari66","lic":"CC0","licUrl":"http://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/deed.en","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kachumber_Salad.JPG"}},"dish/kue-ape":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/kue-ape","n":"Kue ape","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Indonesian cuisine","dot":"#f0b340","intro":[["Kue ape or serabi Jakarta is a popular traditional kue pancake with soft and fluffy center surrounded with thin and crispy crepes, commonly found as a popular street food in Indonesia, especially in Jakarta and other major cities. It is also popularly known as kue cucur tipis (lit: thin cucur), which is different from the thicker kue cucur, and colloquially known as kue tetek (breast cake or boobscake) due to its shape that resembles a nipple. Because it is deemed inappropriate to say ‘tetek’, most Indonesians just say kue ape as in “what cake?”. It is also very similar to serabi Solo."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-kue-ape"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kue_ape"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Indonesian cuisine","cuisine/indonesian-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":4,"links":[["Baking powder","ingredient/baking-powder"],["Coconut milk","ingredient/coconut-milk"],["Pandanus","ingredient/pandanus"],["Wheat flour","ingredient/wheat-flour"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Daily Cooking Quest","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"dailycookingquest.com","note":"Indonesian home cook Anita's blog with a large archive of Indonesian recipes.","url":"https://dailycookingquest.com/cuisines/indonesian.html","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"}]},{"h":"More from Indonesian cuisine","links":[["Arem-arem","dish/arem-arem"],["Arsik","dish/arsik"],["Asam pedas","dish/asam-peda